 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Threshold vs. Rank:** Using a fixed probability threshold instead of rank-based vetoing causes the actual veto rate to vary per scene because base survival rates differ across scenes. Rank vetoing ensures a deterministic peak-population cut [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Timing:** Delaying the veto decision beyond spawn time forfeits the peak-memory benefit because non-surviving spawns are allocated for the delay duration $\Delta$. Waiting until simplification recovers no peak [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Predictor Transfer:** The predictor must be trained on scenes other than the evaluation scene (leave-one-scene-out) to ensure it generalizes. Transfer is harder across domain gaps (e.g., synthetic scenes like MatrixCity) [S1, unofficial].
